  "events": [
    {
      "id": "school-life-content-v1.arrival-library",
      "title": "School arrival scene library",
      "sourceDomain": "school",
      "trigger": [],
      "reactionTriggers": [],
      "priorityClass": "notification",
      "priority": 1,
      "blocking": false,
      "delivery": {
        "policy": "live"
      },
      "cooldownDays": 0,
      "variantCooldownDays": 0,
      "maxShows": 160,
      "conditions": [],
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "literacy",
          "text": "Mara Fen is already arranging slates and points to a badly copied notice. The warm-up is to find the sentence most likely to cost someone money if misunderstood.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "arcana",
          "text": "Ilyra Venn has covered one table with glass, chalk and labels. She asks everyone to touch nothing yet and calls patience the cheapest piece of laboratory equipment.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "rhetoric",
          "text": "Cassian Reed starts before everyone is seated and gives the room ten seconds to decide why his first point is worth hearing.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "etiquette",
          "text": "Eliane Marrow waits beside the doorway instead of the lectern and begins the lesson with the entrance itself.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "field",
          "text": "Rowan Pike leaves a coil of rope in the wrong place on purpose, then asks who noticed it before anyone moved it.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "physical",
          "text": "Tovan Kest checks spacing before the first drill and warns that colliding during warm-up is poor planning rather than enthusiasm.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "arts",
          "text": "Nessa Lark changes the rehearsal-room layout before class and asks what the altered space changes in the performer.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "body",
          "text": "Sera Vey begins with a simple request: stand in a way you can actually maintain rather than a pose meant only to impress.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "continue",
          "label": "Continue",
          "text": "Continue from the School-life presentation.",
          "conditions": [],
          "effects": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "school-life-content-v1.feedback-library",
      "title": "School teacher feedback library",
      "sourceDomain": "school",
      "trigger": [],
      "reactionTriggers": [],
      "priorityClass": "notification",
      "priority": 1,
      "blocking": false,
      "delivery": {
        "policy": "live"
      },
      "cooldownDays": 0,
      "variantCooldownDays": 0,
      "maxShows": 160,
      "conditions": [],
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "mara",
          "text": "Mara marks one line in your notes twice because it is the clearest explanation you wrote, then asks you to simplify the rest without losing the thought.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ilyra",
          "text": "Ilyra asks what observation would have changed your mind, treating uncertainty as part of the lesson rather than a failure.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "cassian",
          "text": "Cassian says the answer improved the moment you stopped performing confidence long enough to listen to the room.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "eliane",
          "text": "Eliane notes that the correction worked because it was small and deliberate instead of a panicked redesign.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "rowan",
          "text": "Rowan points out that finding the clue after being shown the area is useful, but finding the area first is the real goal.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tovan",
          "text": "Tovan notes that the movement looked easier because it was organized better, not because you suddenly tried less.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "nessa",
          "text": "Nessa says she can finally tell what you meant and tells you to keep that intention while refining everything around it.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sera",
          "text": "Sera approves the fact that the choice was deliberate, not whether it matched what someone else would have chosen.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "continue",
          "label": "Continue",
          "text": "Continue from the School-life presentation.",
          "conditions": [],
          "effects": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "school-life-content-v1.peer-context-library",
      "title": "School peer and context scene library",
      "sourceDomain": "school",
      "trigger": [],
      "reactionTriggers": [],
      "priorityClass": "notification",
      "priority": 1,
      "blocking": false,
      "delivery": {
        "policy": "live"
      },
      "cooldownDays": 0,
      "variantCooldownDays": 0,
      "maxShows": 160,
      "conditions": [],
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "notes",
          "text": "A classmate quietly asks to compare notes after the lesson. The exchange stays ordinary social flavor and carries no relationship or progression effect.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "observations",
          "text": "Two students disagree about an observation and are asked to write the other person's interpretation before defending their own.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "switch",
          "text": "Two students practice opposite rhetorical goals and then switch positions halfway through the exercise.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "recovery",
          "text": "A minor etiquette mistake becomes a group exercise in helping someone recover gracefully without drawing more attention to it.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "clues",
          "text": "One student hides an obvious clue and another hides a subtle one, turning the room into a short observation challenge.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "pacing",
          "text": "Students pair by pacing rather than raw strength for a cooperative drill focused on consistency.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "rhythm",
          "text": "The group repeats one short artistic sequence while changing only intention and rhythm.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "care",
          "text": "The class discusses the difference between care, display and conformity without treating any one answer as mandatory.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "continue",
          "label": "Continue",
          "text": "Continue from the School-life presentation.",
          "conditions": [],
          "effects": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "school-life-content-v1.post-lesson-library",
      "title": "School post-lesson reaction library",
      "sourceDomain": "school",
      "trigger": [],
      "reactionTriggers": [],
      "priorityClass": "notification",
      "priority": 1,
      "blocking": false,
      "delivery": {
        "policy": "live"
      },
      "cooldownDays": 0,
      "variantCooldownDays": 0,
      "maxShows": 160,
      "conditions": [],
      "variants": [
        {
          "id": "mara",
          "text": "Mara circles the clearest line in your notes before returning the page.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "ilyra",
          "text": "Ilyra relabels a sample and gives a brief nod when you catch the reason.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "cassian",
          "text": "Cassian calls after you with a better version of your own joke and refuses to admit he had prepared it.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "eliane",
          "text": "Eliane returns a forgotten glove with a dry reminder that preparation is easiest to notice when absent.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "rowan",
          "text": "Rowan asks you to return the practice gear exactly where the next group will expect it.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "tovan",
          "text": "Tovan reminds everyone that recovery is part of training and dismisses the class on time.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "nessa",
          "text": "Nessa changes one note in her rehearsal book after watching your experiment.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "sera",
          "text": "Sera leaves the mirrors uncovered and the lights ordinary for the final quiet exercise.",
          "conditions": [],
          "media": [
            "school.life.classroom.default"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "continue",
          "label": "Continue",
          "text": "Continue from the School-life presentation.",
          "conditions": [],
          "effects": []
        }
      ]
    },
